{"content":[{"c":["AMMINADIB*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Word occurring in some English versions of the ",{"href":"?bref=Song.6.12","r":"Song.6.12","rawR":"Song.6.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Song.6.12","value":"Song.6.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Song of Songs 6:12"},", “or ever I was aware, my soul made me like the chariots of Amminadib” (",{"c":["asv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," mg, ",{"c":["nasb"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," mg). More recent translators have not regarded the term as a proper name. Some proposals for more accurate wording are: “among the chariots of my willing people” (",{"c":["asv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"); “in a chariot beside my prince” (",{"c":["rsv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"); “over the chariots of my noble people” (",{"c":["nasb"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"); and “in my princely bed with my beloved one” (",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Amminadib","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Song of Songs 6:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Song.6.12","rawQueryValue":"Song.6.12","sourceRefExact":"Song.6.12"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"dbc7a02b9ea7526a8c073ff2dd57b30e1af4c5d1eef7c84120fc8d4047016324","sourceItemName":"Amminadib","sourceItemOrder":303,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Amminadib","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Amminadib*","title":"Amminadib*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}